If a patient takes an opioid during at least 1 year then it is possible that a taper continues during some months and it is possible that a taper continues during some years.
If a patient takes an opioid during at least 1 year then it is possible that a taper-duration depends on an opioid-dosage.
Every clinician should individualize a taper with a patient-goal and should individualize a taper with a patient-concern.
